  "title": "What is Coding?",
  "thumbnailUrl": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dqvfgww65/image/upload/v1768150382/fnzlaz2triqkdbfbx8ti.jpg",
  "videoUrl": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dqvfgww65/video/upload/v1768150378/lkhjfpfgysfu48pnoxe7.mp4",
  "description": "Coding is the process of writing specific instructions that tell a computer, smartphone, or software program exactly what to do. Since computers cannot understand human speech, programmers use various programming languages—such as Python, JavaScript, or C++—to act as a translator. These languages allow humans to write logic in a structured way that the computer can then convert into electrical signals to perform tasks, ranging from displaying a simple webpage to launching a rocket.",
