  "description": "HTML (HyperText Markup Language) is the standard language used to create the structure of web pages. It acts as the \"skeleton\" of a website, using tags to define elements like headings, paragraphs, links, and images. While it isn't a programming language that performs complex logic, it is the essential foundation that tells a browser how to display content.",
